hadiths[80]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3004","Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Jibril (peace be upon him) came to me and said: 'I came to you last night, but nothing prevented me from entering the house you were in except that there was a statue of a man in the house, and there was a curtain screen in the house containing images. So order that the head of the statue be cut off so that it becomes like the form of a tree, and order that the screen be cut up.' In another narration: 'There is a screen in the house on the wall in which there are images, so cut off their heads and make them into a floor covering or cushions to be trodden upon, for we do not enter a house in which there are images.' So they were made into two cushions that were trodden upon. 'And order that the dog be taken out.' So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) did so, and the dog turned out to be a puppy belonging to Al-Hasan and Al-Husayn (may Allah be pleased with them both) under a shelf of theirs."" He said: ""He kept enjoining the good treatment of the neighbor upon me until I thought—or I saw—that he would make him an heir."""
