"3065","From Muḥammad ibn Kaʿb, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Unays al-Juhanī: That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Who will take care of Khālid ibn Nubayḥ?"" A man from Hudhayl, and he was at that time near ʿArafah at ʿArnah. ʿAbdullāh ibn Unays said: ""I will, O Messenger of Allah, describe him to me."" He said: ""When you see him, you will be awestruck by him."" He said: ""O Messenger of Allah, by Him Who sent you with the truth, I have never been awestruck by anything ever."" So ʿAbdullāh ibn Unays  set out until he reached the mountains of ʿArafah before the sun set. ʿAbdullāh said: ""I encountered a man and was terrified of him when I saw him, and I recognized him by the terror I felt that he was the one the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had described."" He said to me: ""Who is the man?"" I said: ""A seeker of need; is there a place to spend the night?"" He said: ""Yes, so follow me."" He said: ""So I went in his tracks and prayed ʿAṣr two light rakʿahs, fearing that he might see me. Then I caught up with him and struck him with the sword. Then I departed and came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him."" Muḥammad ibn Kaʿb said: ""So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave him a staff (mikhsarah) and said: 'Lean on this until you meet me, and few are those who lean on staffs.'"" Muḥammad ibn Kaʿb said: ""When ʿAbdullāh ibn Unays  died, he ordered that it be placed on his stomach and his shroud, and he was buried and it was buried with him."""
