"3078","On the authority of ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Fāṭimah (may Allah be pleased with her) and found a curtain at her door, so he did not enter. It was his practice that he would rarely enter without first visiting her. ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) came and found her distressed, so he said: ""What is the matter with you?"" She said: ""The Prophet ﷺ came to me but did not enter."" So ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) went to him and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Fāṭimah was greatly distressed that you came to her but did not enter upon her."" He said: ""What have I to do with the world? And what have I to do with embroidery?"" So he went to Fāṭimah and informed her of the Messenger of Allah's statement. She said: ""Tell the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: What does he command me to do?"" He said: ""Tell her: Let her send it to such-and-such a family."""
"3079","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 3079 Arabic Hadees: 3308"
"3080","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 3080 Arabic Hadees: 100"
"3081","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 3081 Arabic Hadees: 102"
"3082","On the authority of ʿAmr ibn Fulān al-Anṣārī, who said: While he was walking with his lower garment trailing, the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) caught up to him, having taken hold of his own forelock, saying: ""O Allah, Your servant, son of Your servant, son of Your maidservant."" ʿAmr said: I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! I am a man with thin shanks."" He said: ""O ʿAmr! Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has perfected everything He created. O ʿAmr!"" And the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) struck with four fingers of his right hand below ʿAmr's knee, and said: ""O ʿAmr! This is the place of the lower garment."" Then he raised it and placed it below the other [knee] and said: ""O ʿAmr! This is the place of the lower garment."""
"3083","Thawban narrated: The daughter of Hubayrah came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) while she had heavy gold rings on her hand. The Prophet (peace be upon him) began striking her hand. So she went to Fatimah to complain to her. Thawban said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) entered upon Fatimah while I was with him, and she had taken a gold necklace from around her neck. She said: ""This was gifted to me by Abu al-Hasan."" And there was a necklace in her hand. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""O Fatimah, would it please you if people said: 'Fatimah, daughter of Muhammad, has a necklace of fire on her hand?'"" So he left and did not sit. Fatimah then went to the necklace, sold it, bought a slave with its price, and freed her. When this reached the Prophet (peace be upon him), he said: ""Praise be to Allah Who saved Fatimah from the Fire."""
